  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WAVE PERIOD & DIRECTION</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 03:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (NOMADS)<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260926-1900Z-wvperiod<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-26 04:23 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis), 6-hourly cycles</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_direction/legend.png?v=glwu-20260926-1900Z-wvperiod" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Peak wave period (seconds between crests, as filed by GLWU PERPW): <b>LOWEST 0s</b> dark-blue flat &rarr; <b>2</b> blue &rarr; <b>3</b> cyan &rarr; <b>4</b> green &rarr; <b>5</b> yellow &rarr; <b>6</b> orange &rarr; <b>7.5</b> red &rarr; <b>9</b> magenta &rarr; <b>10.5</b> violet &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 12s</b> dark-purple long swell. Same seconds always show the same color; values above 12s stay dark-purple. Arrows point where the waves are traveling (WVDIR filed direction + 180&deg;). Lake max now: <b>5.7s</b>, mean <b>2.6s</b>, mean travel <b>66&deg; (NE)</b>.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — PERPW peak period + WVDIR direction, surface analysis<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260926/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t19z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260926/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t19z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE WAVE PERIOD &amp; DIRECTION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WAVE PERIOD & DIRECTION</h2><p>How far apart the wave crests are right now (peak period, seconds) with arrows showing which way the waves travel. Long-interval swell (high seconds, purple) carries far more energy than short chop at the same height.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_direction/legend.png?v=glwu-20260926-1900Z-wvperiod" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Peak wave period (seconds between crests, as filed by GLWU PERPW): <b>LOWEST 0s</b> dark-blue flat &rarr; <b>2</b> blue &rarr; <b>3</b> cyan &rarr; <b>4</b> green &rarr; <b>5</b> yellow &rarr; <b>6</b> orange &rarr; <b>7.5</b> red &rarr; <b>9</b> magenta &rarr; <b>10.5</b> violet &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 12s</b> dark-purple long swell. Same seconds always show the same color; values above 12s stay dark-purple. Arrows point where the waves are traveling (WVDIR filed direction + 180&deg;). Lake max now: <b>5.7s</b>, mean <b>2.6s</b>, mean travel <b>66&deg; (NE)</b>.</p><p><b>Units:</b> seconds between crests (arrows show travel direction)<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — PERPW peak period + WVDIR direction, surface analysis<br/><b>Update:</b> GLWU 6-hourly cycles (analysis step)<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 03:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260926-1900Z-wvperiod<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-26 04:23 PM EDT<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_glwu.pl">NOMADS GLWU</a></p>]]></description>
